    "done_when": "The node's evidence fragment holds one table row for each of these seventeen plans and no others: a-review-is-sized-to-its-risk, a-small-change-is-a-small-node, a-sprint-closes-on-completable-work, a-sprint-is-live-while-a-crew-works-it, a-stalled-row-says-whether-the-worker-lives, a-window-paces-the-lane, a-worker-can-take-a-brief, a-worker-cannot-write-your-home, a-worker-is-charged-to-a-job, a-worker-knows-it-is-on-compute, a-worker-owns-its-own-record, a-worker-reuses-before-it-writes, advise-the-lane-never-force-it, an-orchestrator-can-discharge-a-refusal, an-orchestrator-cannot-forget-its-obligations, an-orchestrator-is-bound-by-its-inbox, background-agent-fitness-and-dispatch-scope. Each row has: present over checked sections, with a citation for each counted section; the last coordinator; a disposition; and a one-line reason. The fragment states the batch's keep count, which is at most 6. Method, the one the first batch settled after review. A plan's denominator is its implementable sections as reckon's own reader reports them: the section declarations that reckon.mcp._read_plan('reckon', SLUG, view='detail') returns, or the plan-section-declarations meta where present, counting every section declared implementable or done, and counting section 1 only if it is declared implementable. The exact command that prints each plan's denominator appears above the table so a reader can rerun it. Each section counted present cites the file and symbol at main HEAD that shows its deliverable, read with git show; a test file alone is not a citation for a product deliverable. The last coordinator comes from the promotion ledger and live run pointers, marked live when a run for the plan is in flight. The dispositions are keep, merge into a named plan whose scope absorbs it, and close with a one-sentence landed summary. A plan whose deliverables are all present or no longer wanted is close, never keep. A merge target may be a plan in another batch; the final reconciliation resolves chains. The keep budget: the lead has locked the limit at 25 pending plans and four batches of 17 cover 68, so this batch proposes at most 6 keeps, ranked by live, unfinished work, where a live run counts in a plan's favour. Every other plan is merge or close, with a reason saying why it is not in the top six. The first batch's accepted record is docs/evidence/archive/open-work-is-capped-landed.html section triage-first-batch; follow its columns. The node writes only its own evidence fragment and figure directory, edits no plan, names the main HEAD sha it read at in the fragment and the manifest, gives any figure XML-safe characters and parses it with ElementTree, and carries one landing: line in the manifest.",
